# Deploy keys — never commit
.deploy_key
.deploy_key.pub

# Runtime data — keep structure, ignore contents
#
# These are written by the running portal and by scheduled exporters, so a tracked copy
# has two sources of truth. On 2026-08-27 that stopped being theoretical: `git pull` on
# the box refused to run because data/tasks.json held a CC7.3 closure made through the
# UI minutes earlier, and data/patch_servers.json held a fresh fleet export. Accepting
# either incoming version would have destroyed a server-stamped completedAt that exists
# nowhere else.
uploads/*
!uploads/.gitkeep
data/evidence.json
data/change_population.json
data/tasks.json
data/patch_servers.json
data/patch_jobs.json

# Secrets & reminder runtime state — never commit
data/smtp.json
data/reminder_log.json

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Written in place by api/evidence_store.php when evidence is linked to a control or an
# audit test, so a tracked copy is a second source of truth that conflicts with the live one
# on every pull. Untracked 2026-08-27 for the same reason as tasks.json.
data/controls.json
data/audit_tests.json
